  blk/SM is the smallest positive block limit over registers, shared memory, warps
  and blocks; warps and occ follow from it. CUPTI reports blockLimitSharedMem=0 for
  any kernel opting in past the 48 KiB static limit -- it does not model the opt-in
  Triton performs -- so zeros are ignored rather than believed. Its own achieved
  estimate goes to 0 for the same reason, which is why it is not the headline here.
  Times are indicative only: tracing adds overhead, so read the ranking.

